@startuml exclusive-single-key-removal
' ============================================================================
' Exhausting single-key Bag removal after bug 14492: Algorithm 5.60.7 of the
' stack-safety report, section 5.60.7.
'   BLUE   #1565C0  the Bag caller and the preflight (step 0)
'   AMBER  #EF6C00  the exclusivity gate (step 1)
'   GREEN  #2E7D32  the in-place removal inside the fail-stop boundary (steps 2 to 7)
'   PURPLE #6A1B9A  the floor-bounded live prune: one logical edge per iteration
'   GREY   #616161  the unchanged fallback rebuild of section 5.60.2
'   RED    #C62828  refusal before any mutation
' w is the anchor's wrapper count, f its provenance flag, k the key, c its
' count, s the length of its unique suffix, M the Bag's endpoints and B its
' logical bytes. Activity colours use the current form ":label; <<#hex>>".
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ArrowColor #455A64
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontSize 12
  DiamondBorderColor #EF6C00
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3E0
}
skinparam partition {
  BorderColor #2E7D32
  FontColor #1B5E20
}

title <b>Exhausting single-key Bag removal</b>\nin place on an exclusive anchor, by the unchanged rebuild otherwise

start
:""remove_many"" or ""try_remove_many""
of endpoint <latex>k</latex> with count <latex>c</latex>; <<#BBDEFB>>
:**step 0, preflight:** read <latex>c</latex> and check the request; <<#BBDEFB>>
if (request refused?) then (yes)
  :""Err"": the Bag is unchanged; <<#FFCDD2>>
  stop
else (no)
endif
if (does the removal take all <latex>c</latex> copies?) then (no)
  :write the lower count at <latex>k</latex>; <<#BBDEFB>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:**step 1, gate:** ""Arc::get_mut"" succeeds
and the provenance flag is set; <<#FFE0B2>>
if (exclusive: <latex>w = 1 \land f = \mathrm{true}</latex>?) then (Removed)
  partition #E8F5E9 "step 2: fail-stop boundary, catch_unwind: a panic aborts the process" {
    :**step 3,** ""with_write_cursor"":
    ""make_mut"" of a unique ""Arc"" clones nothing; <<#C8E6C9>>
    :**step 4,** ""move_to_existing_value(k)""; <<#C8E6C9>>
    if (<latex>k</latex> is the root or has a child?) then (yes)
      :**step 5,** take the value: ""value_count"" falls by 1,
      the value is disposed, no edge is removed; <<#C8E6C9>>
    else (no: a leaf)
      :**step 5,** ""remove_leaf_with_floor(k, 0)""; <<#E1BEE7>>
      repeat
        :ascend one byte to the parent <latex>q</latex> and decide
        now whether <latex>q</latex> stops the run; <<#E1BEE7>>
        if (<latex>q</latex> holds a real value?) then (no)
          :write a synthetic barrier at <latex>q</latex>; <<#E1BEE7>>
        else (yes)
        endif
        :remove the child's payload and exactly one
        logical edge: a real value is counted out of
        ""value_count"" and disposed, a barrier discarded; <<#E1BEE7>>
      repeat while (<latex>q</latex> at the floor, valued or forked?) is (no) not (yes)
      :retire the barrier at <latex>q</latex> if one was written:
      <latex>s</latex> iterations, as many barriers retired as written; <<#E1BEE7>>
    endif
    :**step 6,** ""normalize_live_empty""; <<#C8E6C9>>
  }
  :**step 7,** ""distinct_len"" falls by 1,
  ""exact_cardinality"" by <latex>c</latex>; <<#C8E6C9>>
  :the same anchor, still exclusive:
  <latex>S = O(1),\ W = O(|k|),\ A = O(s + 1)</latex>; <<#C8E6C9>>
else (Shared)
  :**fallback:** ""*self = self.subtract(&removal)""
  with the one-endpoint Bag ""removal"", the rebuild of 5.60.2; <<#E0E0E0>>
  :a fresh anchor with its flag set; the old anchor's
  final owner drains it: <latex>\Theta(B + M)</latex> in all; <<#E0E0E0>>
endif
stop
@enduml
